<urn:atm:triage:finding/AW5-CI-002>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AW5-CI-002" ;
  triage:title "CI Test (ubuntu-latest) fails: test_cli_parity read/peek envelope mismatch now that the parity test runs in CI" ;
  triage:description "PR #1184 at 1fb8e08cb, ci.yml run 33945711374 job 101251737238: crates/atm-graft-python/tests/test_cli_parity.py::CliParityTests::test_list_read_send_and_ack_match_cli FAILS in _assert_parity (line 284, called from 296): the native read envelope reports action read while the CLI envelope reports action peek and carries additional_match_count; the two dicts differ. The test now executes in CI (closes the ATM-QA-AW5R1-002 gap) and immediately exposes a real AW.5 parity defect between the native typed read result and the CLI read output. Fix the envelope (action name and field set) so native read is byte-equivalent to the CLI, do not weaken the assertion." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-aw" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
